    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Tyler Soderstrom** headlining our core as the most potent play, boasting a 69.25 efficiency score. He draws a high-leverage matchup against Jos\u00e9 Soriano, where a significant 10% park boost combined with a favorable platoon split creates an elite ceiling. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** (67.82) remains an auto-start; while he faces a slight negative platoon adjustment against Connor Prielipp, his raw profile remains indispensable, particularly given our organizational emphasis on speed and high-floor production. **Brice Turang** (61.57) and **Jose Caballero** (61.95) round out the top tier, both benefiting from favorable SP skill metrics\u2014facing pitchers with xERAs north of 4.40\u2014and, in **Jose Caballero**'s case, a wind-out advantage that provides a cushion against his platoon disadvantage.\n\nThe bench selection was headlined by a difficult choice between **Kyle Karros** and our starters. **Kyle Karros** sat at 49.53, narrowly missing the cut behind the stability of **Max Muncy** (50.99). While **Kyle Karros** enjoys a massive 14% park factor boost today, the optimizer favored **Max Muncy** due to his higher base projection and despite the latter\u2019s slight efficiency drag from facing a strong defender. **Austin Riley** also loomed on the bench at 46.45, but with a stiff matchup against Jacob Misiorowski\u2014who carries a 2.70 xERA\u2014the risk of a sub-optimal outcome necessitated keeping him in reserve. We are monitoring **Dalton Rushing**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Alex Freeland**, **James Wood**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Zach McKinstry** closely; all are currently operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status. While historical spots guide these projections, any significant shuffle in the batting order, particularly for leadoff hitters like **Travis Bazzana** or **James Wood**, could trigger a pivot to bench options like **Henry Bolte** or **Cole Young** if the projected scoring drops significantly.",
